From: illogical-impulse <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wayland/lock: destroy native window before removed output

Qt emits screenRemoved while the disappearing QWaylandScreen and wl_output
are still alive. Deferring native window destruction until the next event loop
iteration lets Qt release that wl_output first, leaving the lock surface
attached to a stale protocol object.

Destroy only the QWindow's native Wayland resources synchronously in the
screen-removal callback, then keep deletion of the QML wrapper deferred. This
preserves protocol ordering without deleting a QML object while bindings or
signal handlers may still reference it.
---
 src/wayland/session_lock.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 src/wayland/session_lock.hpp | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/wayland/session_lock.cpp b/src/wayland/session_lock.cpp
index 1ae8d2e..54afa47 100644
--- a/src/wayland/session_lock.cpp
+++ b/src/wayland/session_lock.cpp
@@ -75,0 +76 @@ void WlSessionLock::updateSurfaces(bool show, WlSessionLock* old) {
+			surface->destroyWindow();
@@ -213 +214 @@ WlSessionLockSurface::~WlSessionLockSurface() {
-		this->window->destroy();
+		this->destroyWindow();
@@ -217,0 +219,4 @@ WlSessionLockSurface::~WlSessionLockSurface() {
+void WlSessionLockSurface::destroyWindow() {
+	if (this->window != nullptr) this->window->destroy();
+}
+
diff --git a/src/wayland/session_lock.hpp b/src/wayland/session_lock.hpp
index 9a34eaf..5174ec8 100644
--- a/src/wayland/session_lock.hpp
+++ b/src/wayland/session_lock.hpp
@@ -182,0 +183,2 @@ private:
+	void destroyWindow();
+
@@ -187,0 +190,2 @@ private:
+
+	friend class WlSessionLock;
